title: Metabase Unauthenticated Password Reset SQL Injection
id: 7a3e1b2c-4d5f-6a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects exploitation attempts against CVE-2026-72898, a critical
    SQL injection vulnerability in Metabase's unauthenticated password
    reset endpoint (POST /api/session/reset_password). Attackers send
    crafted input to inject arbitrary SQL into Metabase's application
    database, gaining full administrator access and harvesting
    credentials for all connected data sources.
references:
    - https://cyberpress.org/metabase-zero-day-attack-lets-hackers-gain-admin-access-and-steal-database-credentials/
    - https://gbhackers.com/cisa-warns-critical-metabase-sql-injection-flaw-lets-unauthenticated-attackers-gain-admin-access/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/08/24
tags:
    - attack.t1190
    - attack.t1212
    - attack.t1003
logsource:
    category: webserver
    product: web
detection:
    selection_reset:
        cs-method: 'POST'
        cs-uri|endswith: '/api/session/reset_password'
    selection_sql_patterns:
        cs-uri|contains:
            - 'OR'
            - 'UNION'
            - 'SELECT'
            - 'INSERT'
            - 'UPDATE'
            - 'DELETE'
            - 'DROP'
            - 'EXEC'
            - '--'
            - ';'
    condition: selection_reset and selection_sql_patterns
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate password reset requests with unusual URI parameters
    - Penetration testing against Metabase instances
level: high
